💡 **SUGGESTION: `SessionIoHealth` also notes `notFound` failures — benign file-missing arms the "session IO failing" banner**

`_fsOrThrow` now notes **every** surfaced `Err` into the per-session IO health **before** the error-code mapping (line 277, and the twin in windowed_session_storage.dart:1297) — including `FileErrorCode.notFound`, which this same function maps to `SessionErrorCode.notFound` precisely because it is *not* a storage-health condition.

A genuinely missing path (session deleted by retention/user while a handle is open, a raced `exists` → `open`) is not an fs-health signal, yet it:

1. arms AC5's reclassification — the next stall banner reads `⚠ session IO failing: … restart the host (check open fds / container access)` even though the filesystem is healthy (restart won't help — the levers AC5 set out to stop lying);
2. inflates the `fs-op failures (1m)` gauge on `/stats` and the boot line.

`retryTransientSessionFileIo` already treats notFound as a non-health transient (the #427 REG test asserts a flaky append leaves `SessionIoHealth.lastFailure` null — exhaustion-only surfacing), so the storages are one condition away from consistency:

```dart
if (sessionId != null &&
    error.code != FileErrorCode.notFound) {
  SessionIoHealth.noteFailure(sessionId, text);
}
```

Alternatively, note it but with a distinct label so `stallIsSessionIo` can ignore it. The PR's border-case list covers intermittence and per-session isolation but not this case.
